# samples/01-QuickStart – start it with: dotnet run --project samples/01-QuickStart
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5101

### Seeded: GET /hello/{name}
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/Ada

### 400 – the name is too short (2–30 characters)
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/A

### Same processor, another configuration (shout) and a default for 'name'
GET {{baseUrl}}/greetings?name=Ada

### The definitions, with their status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints

### The registered processors (what the panel offers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints/processors

### Create an endpoint at runtime
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "method": "GET",
  "route": "/ahoy",
  "name": "Ahoy",
  "processor": "greeting",
  "processorConfig": { "greeting": "Ahoy" },
  "parameters": [{ "name": "name", "source": "Query", "maxLength": 30 }]
}

### …and call it
GET {{baseUrl}}/ahoy?name=Jack

### The generated OpenAPI document
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/dynamic.json
